    {
      "sample_id": "MAT212-ba23cb66f16b3ba1",
      "question": "What prerequisites are identified as necessary before studying Taylor and Maclaurin series, and how does the material describe extending Maclaurin’s series to Taylor’s series?",
      "reference_answer": "The prerequisites include having knowledge of power series and the ratio test, being able to differentiate simple functions, and being familiar with the rules for combining power series. Maclaurin’s series is extended to Taylor’s series by combining known power series together.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source_id": "828e92d5-c69c-4d87-b0db-f3fbf971eae3",
          "chunk_id": "4f1c733f-2c0e-4a6e-8bbe-0bf2aa10a1d9",
          "quote": "Prerequisites: Before starting this work you should:\n\n• have knowledge of power series and of the ratio test\n\n• be able to differentiate simple functions\n\n• be familiar with the rules for combining power series",
